A||N||4||reddog||weak and no tail lights||||1||
Z||000000||reddog||12-22-2001||08:26 PM||||Ok....I just started tinkering with my purple GT that I got a few weeks ago. I have a few Electrical problems that I am fairly certain are all inter-related, but would really like the opinion of others with more Fiero Electrical experience.<BR>First...I have no tail lights what so ever!The only thing that is working is the 3rd brake light.<BR>Second.....No Pontiac light<BR>Third......No turn signal. However, the 3rd brake light flashes when you activate the turn signal.And the right side turn signal bulb lights up but is very very dim (does not flash)<BR>Fourth.....The so called "Phantom wipe" occurs from the windshield wipers on start up and when you turn the wheels either right or left. I know that this is a faulty wiper/signal stalk, but is everything else caused by the stalk? Parking lights work on the front, but will not flash. Hazards do not flash either.I checked the fuse block and everything looks good. Any fusable links to the tail lights? Where do they ground?<BR>fifth......A/C not blowing cold(Blower works just no cold air)I thought I read on a past post that the A/C is on the same circuit before the turn signal stalk. Is that true?<BR>Finally.....After turning the ignition off. If you depress the Brake pedal the instrument lights come on!!!never heard of that one.<BR>Any ideas of what it could be, Things to check along with their locations would be helpful. <BR>Scans or pics would be very helpful also<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||12-22-2001||11:40 PM||||Probably a bad ground somewhere.. check the fuses too, one might be blown.<P>As for the A/C, probably needs to be recharged.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/quad_sig_pic_1.jpg">        <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||reddog||12-23-2001||12:36 AM||||Can anyone tell me where g400 or any other related ground is located?<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||12-23-2001||05:07 AM||||The G400 is located under the rear clip on the passenger side. If you don't want to remove it, make a new ground. Splice into one of the black ground wires from one of the blubs and connect it to the frame. To check it just put the wire in the socket and ground it.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg">   <BR>I work where all the missing paperclips go.||||reg||3
Z||000004||4BanGinFun||12-23-2001||05:39 PM||||its more then likely a blown fuse <P>check them all replace them all sometimes they are blown but dont look like it <P>the a/c the condenser could be leaking or the compressor doesnt work or the system just needs to be charged---&gt; get a leak down test first before you recharge it <BR>------------------<BR>85 se 2m4 5spd white<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/flags/canada.gif">   <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/" TARGET=_blank>www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 4BanGinFun (edited 12-23-2001).]||||reg||1
